.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt CONNECT 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm connect
.Nd initiate a connection on a socket
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fn connect "int s" "const struct sockaddr *name" "socklen_t namelen"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn connect
system call connects the socket
.Fa s
to the address
.Fa name ,
of
.Fa namelen
bytes.
.Pp
On a stream or sequenced-packet socket it makes a connection to the
listening socket at
.Fa name .
A local connection completes at once, entering the listener's queue; if
the queue is full,
.Fn connect
fails with
.Er ECONNREFUSED
instead of waiting.
A TCP connection waits for the handshake; on a non-blocking socket
.Fn connect
fails with
.Er EINPROGRESS
instead, the socket becomes writable when the attempt ends, and the
.Dv SO_ERROR
option of
.Xr getsockopt 2
then holds its result.
.Pp
On a datagram socket it sets the destination of sends that give no
address.
A connected UDP socket receives only from that destination, and datagrams
already queued from anyone else are dropped; a local datagram socket still
receives from anyone.
It may be connected again, and connecting to an address of family
.Dv AF_UNSPEC
removes the destination.
.Pp
A UDP or TCP socket that is not bound is bound to an ephemeral port.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EACCES
Search permission is denied on a directory of the path, or write
permission on the socket file.
.It Bq Er EADDRINUSE
No ephemeral port is free.
.It Bq Er EAFNOSUPPORT
The address given for a local socket is not of family
.Dv AF_UNIX .
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa s
is not an open descriptor.
.It Bq Er ECONNREFUSED
No socket is bound to the local name, it is not listening, or its queue is
full; or the TCP peer refused the connection.
.It Bq Er EHOSTUNREACH
The IPv4 destination cannot be reached.
.It Bq Er EINPROGRESS
The socket is non-blocking and the TCP connection cannot be completed at
once.
.It Bq Er EINTR
A signal interrupted a TCP connection attempt; it is not restarted, even
with
.Dv SA_RESTART .
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The address is too short or malformed, a local socket was given an unnamed
address, or the local socket is listening.
.It Bq Er EISCONN
The stream or sequenced-packet socket is already connected, or the TCP
socket is connecting or listening.
.It Bq Er ENAMETOOLONG
The path is 108 bytes or longer.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
Nothing exists at the path.
.It Bq Er ENOTDIR
A component of the path prefix is not a directory.
.It Bq Er ENOTSOCK
.Fa s
is not a socket, or the path names a file that is not a socket.
.It Bq Er EPROTOTYPE
The local socket named is of another type.
.It Bq Er ETIMEDOUT
The TCP handshake went unanswered.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr accept 2 ,
.Xr getpeername 2 ,
.Xr getsockopt 2 ,
.Xr listen 2 ,
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr unix 4
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn connect
system call conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn connect
system call first appeared in
.Bx 4.2 .
